      "title": "Troubleshooting Webhook Engine Environment Variable Overrides",
      "content_summary": "Addresses issues where configuration changes or feature flags fail to apply due to conflicting or incorrect environment variables in the Webhook Engine.",
      "content_body": "When Webhook Engine updates or feature flags do not take effect, check for environment variables that may be overriding the current configuration file. A common root cause is a stale `WH_FEATURE_FLAG` variable or a mismatched environment name pointing to the wrong config set. To resolve, audit the deployment manifest and ensure the active environment variables align with the intended configuration. If the issue stems from a policy misconfiguration, correct the policy and redeploy the service."
